saying, Is this the man that made the earth to tremble, that did shake kingdoms;

translated_text:
The burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste,
and brought to silence; because in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste,
and brought to silence;

original_text:
The burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste,
and brought to silence; because in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste,
and brought to silence;

translated_text:
Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make
an agreement with me
by a present, and come out to me: and eat ye every one of his vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his own cistern;

original_text:
Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make
an agreement with me
by a present, and come out to me: and eat ye every one of his vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his own cistern;

translated_text:
Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou
wast not spoiled; and dealest treacherously, and they dealt not treacherously with thee! when thou shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt be spoiled;
and when thou shalt make an end to deal treacherously, they shall deal treacherously with thee.

original_text:
Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou
wast not spoiled; and dealest treacherously, and they dealt not treacherously with thee! when thou shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt be spoiled;
and when thou shalt make an end to deal treacherously, they shall deal treacherously with thee.

translated_text:
Or let him take hold of my strength,
that he may make peace with me;
and he shall make peace with me.

original_text:
Or let him take hold of my strength,
that he may make peace with me;
and he shall make peace with me.

translated_text:
From the sole of the foot even unto the head
there is no soundness in it;
but wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.

original_text:
From the sole of the foot even unto the head
there is no soundness in it;
but wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.

translated_text:
Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with;
it is
 iniquity, even the solemn meeting.

original_text:
Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with;
it is
 iniquity, even the solemn meeting.

translated_text:
And
at what instant I shall speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to build and to plant
it;

original_text:
And
at what instant I shall speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to build and to plant
it;

translated_text:
Because my people hath forgotten me, they have burned incense to vanity, and they have caused them to stumble in their ways
from the ancient paths, to walk in paths,
in a way not cast up;

original_text:
Because my people hath forgotten me, they have burned incense to vanity, and they have caused them to stumble in their ways
from the ancient paths, to walk in paths,
in a way not cast up;

translated_text:
Thus saith the LORD, The people
which were left of the sword found grace in the wilderness;
even Israel, when I went to cause him to rest.

original_text:
Thus saith the LORD, The people
which were left of the sword found grace in the wilderness;
even Israel, when I went to cause him to rest.

translated_text:
The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, that
was
 the first year of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon;

original_text:
The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, that
was
 the first year of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon;

translated_text:
How long shall
this be in the heart of the prophets that prophesy lies? yea,
they are prophets of the deceit of their own heart;

original_text:
How long shall
this be in the heart of the prophets that prophesy lies? yea,
they are prophets of the deceit of their own heart;

translated_text:
I spake unto thee in thy prosperity;
but thou saidst, I will not hear. This
hath been thy manner from thy youth, that thou obeyedst not my voice.

original_text:
I spake unto thee in thy prosperity;
but thou saidst, I will not hear. This
hath been thy manner from thy youth, that thou obeyedst not my voice.

translated_text:
Thou
art my battle axe
and weapons of war: for with thee will I break in pieces the nations, and with thee will I destroy kingdoms;

original_text:
Thou
art my battle axe
and weapons of war: for with thee will I break in pieces the nations, and with thee will I destroy kingdoms;

translated_text:
And joy and gladness is taken from the plentiful field, and from the land of Moab; and I have caused wine to fail from the winepresses: none shall tread with shouting;
their shouting
shall be no shouting.

original_text:
And joy and gladness is taken from the plentiful field, and from the land of Moab; and I have caused wine to fail from the winepresses: none shall tread with shouting;
their shouting
shall be no shouting.

translated_text:
Now when all the captains of the forces which
were in the fields,
even they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed unto him men, and women, and children, and of the poor of the land, of them that were not carried away captive to Babylon;

original_text:
Now when all the captains of the forces which
were in the fields,
even they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed unto him men, and women, and children, and of the poor of the land, of them that were not carried away captive to Babylon;

translated_text:
Likewise when all the Jews that
were in Moab, and among the Ammonites, and in Edom, and that
were in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan;

original_text:
Likewise when all the Jews that
were in Moab, and among the Ammonites, and in Edom, and that
were in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan;

translated_text:
They cried unto them, Depart ye;
it is unclean; depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, they said among the heathen, They shall no more sojourn
there.

original_text:
They cried unto them, Depart ye;
it is unclean; depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, they said among the heathen, They shall no more sojourn
there.

translated_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD;
Art thou he of whom I have spoken in old time by my servants the prophets of Israel, which prophesied in those days
many years that I would bring thee against them?

original_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD;
Art thou he of whom I have spoken in old time by my servants the prophets of Israel, which prophesied in those days
many years that I would bring thee against them?

translated_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they say unto you, Thou
land
 devourest up men, and hast bereaved thy nations;

original_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they say unto you, Thou
land
 devourest up men, and hast bereaved thy nations;

translated_text:
Say now to the rebellious house, Know ye not what these
things mean? tell
them, Behold, the king of Babylon is come to Jerusalem, and hath taken the king thereof, and the princes thereof, and led them with him to Babylon;

original_text:
Say now to the rebellious house, Know ye not what these
things mean? tell
them, Behold, the king of Babylon is come to Jerusalem, and hath taken the king thereof, and the princes thereof, and led them with him to Babylon;

translated_text:
This
city shall not be your caldron, neither shall ye be the flesh in the midst thereof;
but I will judge you in the border of Israel:

original_text:
This
city shall not be your caldron, neither shall ye be the flesh in the midst thereof;
but I will judge you in the border of Israel:

translated_text:
For thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast clapped
thine
 hands, and stamped with the feet, and rejoiced in heart with all thy despite against the land of Israel;

original_text:
For thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast clapped
thine
 hands, and stamped with the feet, and rejoiced in heart with all thy despite against the land of Israel;

translated_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the Philistines have dealt by revenge, and have taken vengeance with a despiteful heart, to destroy
it
 for the old hatred;

original_text:
Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the Philistines have dealt by revenge, and have taken vengeance with a despiteful heart, to destroy
it
 for the old hatred;

translated_text:
Yet also I lifted up my hand unto them in the wilderness, that I would not bring them into the land which I had given
them, flowing with milk and honey, which
is the glory of all lands;

original_text:
Yet also I lifted up my hand unto them in the wilderness, that I would not bring them into the land which I had given
them, flowing with milk and honey, which
is the glory of all lands;

translated_text:
Son of man, set thy face toward the south, and drop
thy word
 toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the south field;

original_text:
Son of man, set thy face toward the south, and drop
thy word
 toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the south field;

translated_text:
And when I looked, behold, an hand
was sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book
was therein;

original_text:
And when I looked, behold, an hand
was sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book
was therein;

translated_text:
For thou
art not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language,
but to the house of Israel;

original_text:
For thou
art not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language,
but to the house of Israel;

translated_text:
Then I would know the truth of the fourth beast, which was diverse from all the others, exceeding dreadful, whose teeth
were of iron, and his nails
of brass;
which devoured, brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with his feet;

original_text:
Then I would know the truth of the fourth beast, which was diverse from all the others, exceeding dreadful, whose teeth
were of iron, and his nails
of brass;
which devoured, brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with his feet;

translated_text:
And whereas the king saw a watcher and an holy one coming down from heaven, and saying, Hew the tree down, and destroy it; yet leave the stump of the roots thereof in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and
let his portion
be with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him;

original_text:
