well: but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who
is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?

translated_text:
So I bought her to me for fifteen
pieces of silver, and
for an homer of barley, and an half homer of barley:

original_text:
So I bought her to me for fifteen
pieces of silver, and
for an homer of barley, and an half homer of barley:

translated_text:
Plead with your mother, plead: for she
is not my wife, neither
am I her husband: let her therefore put away her whoredoms out of her sight, and her adulteries from between her breasts;

original_text:
Plead with your mother, plead: for she
is not my wife, neither
am I her husband: let her therefore put away her whoredoms out of her sight, and her adulteries from between her breasts;

translated_text:
Who knoweth
if he will return and repent, and leave a blessing behind him;
even a meat offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?

original_text:
Who knoweth
if he will return and repent, and leave a blessing behind him;
even a meat offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?

translated_text:
Therefore their goods shall become a booty, and their houses a desolation: they shall also build houses, but not inhabit
them;
 and they shall plant vineyards, but not drink the wine thereof.

original_text:
Therefore their goods shall become a booty, and their houses a desolation: they shall also build houses, but not inhabit
them;
 and they shall plant vineyards, but not drink the wine thereof.

translated_text:
And flocks shall lie down in the midst of her, all the beasts of the nations: both the cormorant and the bittern shall lodge in the upper lintels of it;
their voice shall sing in the windows; desolation
shall be in the thresholds: for he shall uncover the cedar work.

original_text:
